\pard\qc\sa160\f1\fs34\b\cf1 Administrator Access Required\par
\pard\qc\sa220\f0\fs22\b0\cf2 Power BI Lineage Application\par

\pard\sa140\f0\fs22\cf0
The application currently uses personal credentials. To move it to an organization-controlled setup, please provide the following required access and configuration.\par

\pard\sa130\fs25\b\cf1 1. Microsoft Entra ID Accounts\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab A dedicated, non-personal Power BI account with a Power BI Premium Per User license.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Add this account to the required Power BI workspaces, Apps, and App Audiences.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Create an automation service principal for Power BI REST APIs and XMLA access. Suggested name: PBI-Lineage-Automation-SP.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Create a read-only admin metadata service principal. Suggested name: PBI-Lineage-AdminAPI-SP. A separate identity is preferred for audit and least-privilege access.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Use certificates for production credentials where possible.\par

\pard\sa130\fs25\b\cf1 2. Power BI API and Tenant Access\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Grant admin consent for the delegated Power BI API permissions listed in the attached permission sheet.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Allow the approved service principals or security groups to use Power BI APIs.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Allow the admin metadata service principal to use read-only admin APIs.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Enable the Dataset Execute Queries REST API.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Enable XMLA read access for semantic-model metadata and lineage.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Allow report-definition or PBIX download where required for visual-level lineage.\par

\pard\sa130\fs25\b\cf1 3. Power BI Workspace and Semantic Model Access\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Add the automation service principal or approved security group to all target workspaces.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Grant Viewer and Build access at minimum. Grant an approved higher role only where XMLA or report-definition access requires it.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Grant Build access to every semantic model the application must inspect.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab For reports using semantic models from other workspaces, grant access to those source workspaces and semantic models as well.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Provide the approved workspace names and IDs, App names and IDs, and App Audience mappings.\par

\pard\sa130\fs25\b\cf1 4. Windows Deployment Environment\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab A supported 64-bit Windows Server or Windows host.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Python 3.11 and the application dependencies.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Windows COM/OLE DB support, adodbapi, and the Microsoft MSOLAP provider for XMLA access.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab An approved Windows service account to run the application.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Required outbound HTTPS access, certificates, application port or reverse proxy, logging, and automatic restart configuration.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab MSOLAP download: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/analysis-services/client-libraries\par

\pard\sa130\fs25\b\cf1 5. Snowflake Enterprise Access\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab A Snowflake Enterprise account or approved organization account.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab A dedicated Snowflake service account and application role.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab A database, schema, warehouse, and stage or repository for the application.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Permission for the application role to create the approved tables, views, procedures, functions, secrets, and Streamlit objects in the application schema.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Read access to the required Snowflake metadata and lineage objects.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Network rules for login.microsoftonline.com, api.powerbi.com, api.anthropic.com, and any approved internal API gateway.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab An External Access Integration assigned to the Streamlit application.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab API integration or external-function objects if the approved architecture uses external functions.\par

\pard\sa130\fs25\b\cf1 6. Claude Access\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab An approved Claude API key stored in the organization secret-management system.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab The approved Claude model and configuration for each environment: Development, Test, UAT, and Production as applicable.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Approved agent names, roles, instructions, tools, and usage limits.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Agents linked to the correct application session, with session isolation, expiry, persistence, and audit rules.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Outbound HTTPS access to the approved Claude or Anthropic API endpoint.\par

\pard\sa130\fs25\b\cf1 7. Secure Configuration to Provide\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Microsoft Entra tenant ID.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Client IDs and certificate or secret references for both service principals.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Dedicated Power BI account UPN and confirmation of the PPU license.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Power BI security-group names and approved workspace and App IDs.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Snowflake account identifier, role, warehouse, database, schema, Streamlit object, secret names, and External Access Integration name.\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa55\fs22 \bullet\tab Claude environment, model, agent list, session-linking configuration, and secret reference.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Provide all credentials and secrets through the approved secure channel, not in email or plaintext.\par

\pard\sa150\fs25\b\cf1 Completion Confirmation\b0\cf0\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] Entra accounts and app registrations are ready.\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] API permissions and admin consent are complete.\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] Power BI tenant settings and security groups are configured.\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] Workspace, semantic model, App, and Audience access is granted.\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] Windows host and dependencies are ready.\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] Snowflake objects, role, network rules, and integrations are ready.\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] Claude access, agents, and session configuration are ready.\par
\pard\li180\sa50\fs22 [ ] All secrets are stored securely and available to the application.\par
}
